<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Tri-tiltrotor VTOL with a conventional empennage.

  Three tilting rotors carry the VTOL and the transition: two above the main wing and
  one on the tail boom. Behind the wing sits a real tail assembly - a horizontal
  stabiliser with two elevators under the rear rotor, and a fin with a rudder - which
  is what does the aerodynamic work in forward flight.

  Pitch in hover comes from plain thrust differential between the wing pair and the
  rear rotor (2 * T_front * 0.22 = T_rear * 0.65), the same mechanism as the
  tiltrotor_2plus1 model, so no change to PX4's control allocation is needed. That is
  the reason all three rotors tilt rather than the tail carrying a fixed pusher:
  ActuatorEffectivenessTiltrotorVTOL writes every rotor's thrust *magnitude* into the
  z row of the effectiveness matrix regardless of where the rotor points
  (ActuatorEffectivenessRotors.cpp), taking direction to come from the shared
  collective tilt, so a fixed forward-facing rotor gets allocated as if it lifted.

  The wing rotors sit at x = 0.27, y = +-0.35, on pylons that reach FORWARD past the
  wing leading edge (2026-08-31, step 143). This is the classic tiltrotor nacelle
  layout and it is forced by geometry, not preference.

  At the old station (x = 0.22, y = +-0.25) the 129.4 mm disc swept THROUGH the
  x8_wing centre pod. Two things hid this for a long time:
    1. base_link's collision box (0.55 x 2.144 x 0.05, z -0.160..-0.110) does not
       represent the mesh at all ; the mesh spans z -0.100..+0.208 and the pod
       (half-width 0.20 m, reaching x = +0.288) is absent from it. Any box-based
       clearance check therefore reported ~65 mm where the truth was 0 mm.
    2. The first mesh-based check measured distance to mesh VERTICES. Vertex spacing
       here is ~21 mm, so a disc entering the surface between vertices read as
       "32.8 mm clear". cad/dogrula.py, which does a real solid boolean, kept
       reporting penetration and was right. check_model_clearance.py now samples
       triangles by area (~1.5 mm) and models the disc's 10.6 mm thickness.

  Why x = 0.27 and not a span move: at 90 deg tilt the disc is a VERTICAL plane. Any
  hub behind the local leading edge cuts the wing chord, and sweep means going
  outboard pushes x further aft ; so no station along the span works while the pylon
  sits on the wing (measured: 0.0 mm at every y from 0.35 to 0.70). Shrinking the prop
  does not help either (0.0 mm even at 170 mm diameter) because the disc PLANE, not
  its radius, is what is inside the wing. Raising the pylon works but needs +80 mm,
  which moves r_z ; the exact quantity whose change broke back-transition when the
  tail rotor was raised (step 132). Moving the hub ahead of the leading edge is the
  only fix that leaves r_z untouched: 32.8 mm clear, verified by both the triangle
  sampler and cad/dogrula.py (front rotors clean at all tilt angles for the first time).

  Cost: arm_ratio = 2*ROTOR_PX[0]/|ROTOR_PX[2]| rises 0.677 -> 0.831, so the hover
  split shifts (auto-derived in TiltrotorIndiControl.hpp, no separate constant).
  r_z and the tail arm are unchanged.
  They were moved from below the wing to above it on 2026-08-02; the pylon/motor/rotor
  stack was mirrored about the wing, keeping the model's existing 0.0075 m prop-above-
  motor clearance (the same rule the tail rotor follows). NOTE: rotor z feeds
  tiltrotor_indi::ROTOR_PZ in the PX4 controller with an FLU->FRD sign flip, so that
  array must track this file; see the comment at the rotor links below.
  Further outboard the wing ends sooner - at y = +-0.35 it stops at x = 0.20 - which
  is why the 2+1 model needs forward columns to reach its rotors.

  Wing, propeller and elevon meshes and the aerodynamic coefficients are reused from
  the standard_vtol / tiltrotor / tiltrotor_2plus1 models, none of which are modified.
-->
<sdf version='1.5'>
  <model name='tiltrotor_tailplane'>
    <pose>0 0 0.246 0 0 0</pose>
    <link name='base_link'>
      <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
      <inertial>
        <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
        <mass>5</mass>
        <!-- Wingspan is the tri-tiltrotor's, so ixx is close to its 0.197563. iyy/izz
             go up from that model's 0.2: the tail assembly adds roughly 0.1 kg of
             stabiliser and fin about 0.7 m aft, worth m*r^2 ~ 0.05 about both the
             pitch and yaw axes. The stabiliser's own span contributes ~0.002 to ixx,
             which is inside the noise. -->
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.2</ixx>
          <ixy>0</ixy>
          <ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>0.25</iyy>
          <iyz>0</iyz>
          <izz>0.25</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
        <!-- RUZGAR ETKISI (2026-08-31, adim 135). ONCEDEN YOKTU: model
             hicbir link'inde <enable_wind> tasimadigi icin dunyadaki <wind>
             ayari bu araca HIC uygulanmiyordu - yani butun SITL dogrulamalari
             SIFIR RUZGARDA yapilmisti. Gercek bir ucusun en yaygin bozucusu
             modelde yoktu.
             MATLAB plant'i (tiltrotor_plant_deriv.m) rüzgari zaten destekliyor
             (wind_ned girisi, v_rel = vel_b - wind_b), yani bu ekleme iki
             ortami da ayni bozucuya maruz birakir. -->
        <enable_wind>true</enable_wind>
      <!-- GOVDE/KANAT temas kutusu. INIS TAKIMI 2026-08-30'da (adim 133)
           EKLENENE KADAR yere temas eden TEK sey buydu: araç gövdesinin
           altındaki düz bir levha, süspansiyonsuz. Ölçülen sonucu, kovalanan
           iniş sorununun ta kendisi: temas anında pitch açısal ivmesi tek
           tikte 40.8 rad/s^2'ye fırlıyordu (adım 119). Levha KALDI (kanat
           gerçekten oradadır ve yan yatışta değer), ama artık ilk temas
           bacaklara düşüyor.
           SURTUNME ARTIK TANIMLI: <ode/> bostu, yani Gazebo varsayilani
           (mu = 1.0) kullaniliyordu — kompozit bir kanat yuzeyi icin fazla
           yapiskan. mu/mu2 = 0.6/0.5 kuru asfalt-kompozit mertebesi. -->
      <collision name='base_link_collision'>
        <pose>-0.01 0 -0.135 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.55 2.144 0.05</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <surface>
          <contact>
            <ode>
              <kp>100000</kp>
              <kd>1.0</kd>
              <max_vel>0.1</max_vel>
              <min_depth>0.001</min_depth>
            </ode>
          </contact>
          <friction>
            <ode>
              <mu>0.6</mu>
              <mu2>0.5</mu2>
            </ode>
          </friction>
        </surface>
      </collision>
      <visual name='base_link_visual'>
        <pose>0.53 -1.072 -0.1 1.5707963268 0 3.1415926536</pose>
        <geometry>
          <mesh>
            <scale>0.001 0.001 0.001</scale>
            <uri>model://standard_vtol/meshes/x8_wing.dae</uri>
          </mesh>
        </geometry>
        <material> <!-- DarkGrey-->
          <ambient>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <!-- Tail boom carrying the rear rotor and the empennage. -->
      <!-- Kuyruk motor pilonu (2026-08-30, adim 132). Motor 0.045 -> 0.135'e
           yukseldi, arada 9 cm bosluk kaldi; bu gorsel onu dolduruyor.
           NEDEN MOTOR YUKSELDI: 0.10 m yaricapli disk 90 dereceye donerken alt
           ucu z = motor_z - 0.10'a iniyor. Eski motor_z = 0.045 ile bu -0.055
           demekti — yani disk cubugun (ust yuzu +0.030) ve yatay kuyrugun
           (+-0.040) ICINDEN geciyordu. Cubugu temizlemek icin motor_z > 0.130
           sart. Olculdu: check_model_clearance.py. -->
      <!-- INIS TAKIMI (2026-08-30, adim 133). ONCEDEN HIC YOKTU: arac
           govdesinin altindaki duz levhayla yere oturuyordu ve olculen temas
           darbesi tek tikte 40.8 rad/s^2 pitch ivmesiydi (adim 119) — yani
           kovalanan "sert temas" arizasinin fiziksel karsiligi modelin
           kendisindeydi, kontrolcude degil.
           UC AYAK, ucgen yerlesim: iki on ayak rotor istasyonlarinda
           (x = +0.22, y = +-0.25; adim 143'te motorlar disa alindi ama
           AYAKLAR YERINDE KALDI: o istasyonda kanat hala var, LE = +0.254),
           bir kuyruk ayagi (x = -0.62). Ucu da
           z = -0.20'ye kadar iner, yani govde levhasindan (z = -0.16 alt yuz)
           4 cm asagida — ilk temas HER ZAMAN bacaklara duser.
           kp dusuruldu (100000 -> 30000) ve kd yukseltildi (1.0 -> 5.0):
           gercek bir inis takimi yaylanir, rijit bir kutu yaylanmaz. Bu,
           temas darbesini yumusatan asil parametredir.
           NOT: ayaklar base_link'in COLLISION'idir, ayri link DEGIL — ayri
           link olsaydi eklem ve atalet gerekirdi ve kutle butcesi degisirdi.
           Gorsel karsiliklari da eklendi ki GUI'de gorulsun. -->
      <collision name='leg_front_right_collision'>
        <pose>0.22 -0.25 -0.175 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.012</radius>
            <length>0.05</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <surface>
          <contact>
            <ode>
              <kp>12000</kp>
              <kd>25.0</kd>
              <max_vel>0.02</max_vel>
              <min_depth>0.003</min_depth>
            </ode>
          </contact>
          <friction>
            <ode>
              <mu>0.9</mu>
              <mu2>0.9</mu2>
            </ode>
          </friction>
        </surface>
      </collision>
      <visual name='leg_front_right_visual'>
        <pose>0.22 -0.25 -0.175 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.012</radius>
            <length>0.05</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.1 0.1 0.1 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1.0</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <collision name='leg_front_left_collision'>
        <pose>0.22 0.25 -0.175 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.012</radius>
            <length>0.05</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <surface>
          <contact>
            <ode>
              <kp>12000</kp>
              <kd>25.0</kd>
              <max_vel>0.02</max_vel>
              <min_depth>0.003</min_depth>
            </ode>
          </contact>
          <friction>
            <ode>
              <mu>0.9</mu>
              <mu2>0.9</mu2>
            </ode>
          </friction>
        </surface>
      </collision>
      <visual name='leg_front_left_visual'>
        <pose>0.22 0.25 -0.175 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.012</radius>
            <length>0.05</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.1 0.1 0.1 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1.0</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <collision name='leg_tail_collision'>
        <pose>-0.62 0.0 -0.175 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.012</radius>
            <length>0.05</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <surface>
          <contact>
            <ode>
              <kp>12000</kp>
              <kd>25.0</kd>
              <max_vel>0.02</max_vel>
              <min_depth>0.003</min_depth>
            </ode>
          </contact>
          <friction>
            <ode>
              <mu>0.9</mu>
              <mu2>0.9</mu2>
            </ode>
          </friction>
        </surface>
      </collision>
      <visual name='leg_tail_visual'>
        <pose>-0.62 0.0 -0.175 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <cylinder>
            <radius>0.012</radius>
            <length>0.05</length>
          </cylinder>
        </geometry>
        <material>
          <ambient>0.1 0.1 0.1 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.1 0.1 0.1 1.0</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <!-- INCELTILDI 0.04 -> 0.02 (2026-08-30, adim 132). Ust yuzu +0.030'dan
           +0.010'a indi. Kuyruk rotor diskinin 90 derecede alt ucu z = 0.035'e
           iniyor; eski cubuk ust yuzuyle temas ediyordu. Inceltmek, motor
           pilonunu 12 cm yerine 9 cm'de tutmayi mumkun kildi — pilon ne kadar
           uzunsa egilme/titresim riski o kadar buyuk (kullanici uyarisi). -->
      <visual name='tail_boom'>
        <!-- UZATILDI 0.62 -> 0.71 m, merkez -0.50 -> -0.545 (2026-08-31,
             adim 139). Fin adim 133'te -0.74'ten -0.86'ya tasindi ama cubuk
             -0.81'de bitiyordu: fin cubugun ucundan 5 cm TASIYORDU, yani
             gercek aracta tabani desteklenmeyen bir konsol. Simulasyonda
             isirmaz (rijit govde) ama gercekte titresim ve yorulma yaratir.
             Yeni cubuk -0.95..-0.19; fin (-0.94..-0.78) artik tamamen
             cubugun uzerinde oturuyor. Ilk denemede 0.71 m verilmisti ve fin
             hala 4 cm tasiyordu - olcum yakaladi. -->
        <pose>-0.545 0 -0.01 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.71 0.04 0.02</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material> <!-- DarkGrey-->
          <ambient>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <!-- Horizontal stabiliser, slung under the rear rotor. Its 0.11 m of clearance
           below the rotor disc keeps the two from intersecting through the tilt sweep. -->
      <visual name='tailplane'>
        <pose>-0.70 0 -0.04 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.16 0.60 0.012</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material> <!-- DarkGrey-->
          <ambient>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <!-- Strut tying the stabiliser to the boom. -->
      <visual name='tailplane_strut'>
        <!-- Strut'un ust yuzu cubugun ust yuzuyle HIZALI (z=0.000).
             ONCEDEN z -0.015 merkez / 0.06 boy idi, yani ust yuzu +0.015'te
             ve cubugun 15 mm USTUNE tasiyordu. Fin -0.90/z0.12'deyken zararsizdi
             (5 mm bosluk); fin -0.78/z0.10'a alininca (alt kenar 0.000) 4.9 cm^3
             GIRISIM olustu ; cad/dogrula.py yakaladi. Strut'un tek isi
             tailplane'i cubuga baglamak; cubugun ustune tasmasinin islevi yok. -->
        <pose>-0.70 0 -0.0225 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.05 0.03 0.045</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material> <!-- DarkGrey-->
          <ambient>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <!-- Fin. -->
      <!-- GERIYE ALINDI -0.74 -> -0.86 (2026-08-30, adim 132). OLCULEN SORUN:
           tilt = 0'da (yani HOVER'IN TAMAMINDA) kuyruk rotor diski yatay olarak
           z = 0.07'de duruyor ve fin z = 0.02..0.22 araligini kapliyor — disk
           dogrudan fininin ICINDEN geciyordu. Bu, tilt araligini sinirlayarak
           COZULEMEZ, cunku carpisma en dusuk tilt'te olusuyor; olculdu.
           Fin KALDIRILMADI, cunku sabit kanat fazinda (16 m/s, rudder kalici
           kapali — adim 77) yon kararliligini saglayan tek yapi odur.
           Geriye almak kolu da uzatiyor: SURF_CPX[4] -0.74 -> -0.95, yaw
           kararliligi %28 artar. -->
      <visual name='vertical_stabiliser'>
        <pose>-0.78 0 0.10 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.16 0.02 0.2</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material> <!-- DarkGrey-->
          <ambient>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <!-- Pylons rising from the wing to the tilt rotors. At the rotor station
           (x = 0.185, y = +-0.35, adim 143) the wing's upper surface sits at z = +0.0160,
           measured off x8_wing.dae by plane section. At the OLD station (0.205, 0.25) it
           was +0.0188; the 2026-08-02 ray cast read +0.0136 there.
           Each pylon spans z = +0.010 .. +0.070, so its foot is buried ~4 mm into the
           wing skin and its head meets the motor body, which starts at +0.0675.

           SHORTENED 0.05 -> 0.03 AND MOVED FORWARD 0.22 -> 0.205 (2026-08-30,
           step 132). MEASURED PROBLEM: at FULL TILT (90 deg — the fixed-wing
           cruise attitude, which the mission actually flies) the rotor disc
           SWEPT THROUGH ITS OWN PYLON. The disc is vertical there and sits at
           x = 0.245 (the rotor hub is 0.025 above the tilt axis, so tilting 90
           deg moves it 0.025 aft->fwd); the old pylon's aft face was at exactly
           x = 0.245. Clearance was 0.0 mm through the whole cruise phase.
           WHY SHORTEN AND NOT RAISE THE MOTOR: raising was measured too and is
           far worse — +9.5 cm of pylon buys only 10 mm, while shortening buys
           25 mm and costs NOTHING: the pylon is pure structure, absent from both
           the aero model (no LiftDrag) and the control model (not in the
           effectiveness matrix). Re-check with check_model_clearance.py. -->
      <visual name='right_motor_pylon'>
        <pose>0.2175 -0.35 0.04 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.105 0.03 0.06</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material> <!-- DarkGrey-->
          <ambient>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <visual name='left_motor_pylon'>
        <pose>0.2175 0.35 0.04 0 0 0</pose>
        <geometry>
          <box>
            <size>0.105 0.03 0.06</size>
          </box>
        </geometry>
        <material> <!-- DarkGrey-->
          <ambient>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</ambient>
          <diffuse>0.175 0.175 0.175 1.0</diffuse>
        </material>
      </visual>
      <gravity>1</gravity>
      <velocity_decay />
      <self_collide>0</self_collide>

      <sensor name="imu_sensor" type="imu">
        <gz_frame_id>base_link</gz_frame_id>
        <always_on>1</always_on>
        <update_rate>250</update_rate>
        <imu>
          <angular_velocity>
            <x>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.0003394</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>3.8785e-05</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>1000</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </x>
            <y>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.0003394</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>3.8785e-05</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>1000</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </y>
            <z>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.0003394</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>3.8785e-05</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>1000</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </z>
          </angular_velocity>
          <linear_acceleration>
            <x>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.004</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>0.006</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>300</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </x>
            <y>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.004</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>0.006</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>300</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </y>
            <z>
              <noise type="gaussian">
                <mean>0</mean>
                <stddev>0.004</stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_stddev>0.006</dynamic_bias_stddev>
                <dynamic_bias_correlation_time>300</dynamic_bias_correlation_time>
              </noise>
            </z>
          </linear_acceleration>
        </imu>
      </sensor>
      <sensor name="air_pressure_sensor" type="air_pressure">
        <gz_frame_id>base_link</gz_frame_id>
        <always_on>1</always_on>
        <update_rate>50</update_rate>
        <air_pressure>
          <pressure>
            <noise type="gaussian">
              <mean>0</mean>
              <stddev>0.01</stddev>
            </noise>
          </pressure>
        </air_pressure>
      </sensor>
      <sensor name="magnetometer_sensor" type="magnetometer">
        <gz_frame_id>base_link</gz_frame_id>
        <always_on>1</always_on>
        <update_rate>100</update_rate>
        <magnetometer>
          <x>
            <noise type="gaussian">
              <stddev>0.0001</stddev>
            </noise>
          </x>
          <y>
            <noise type="gaussian">
              <stddev>0.0001</stddev>
            </noise>
          </y>
          <z>
            <noise type="gaussian">
              <stddev>0.0001</stddev>
            </noise>
          </z>
        </magnetometer>
      </sensor>
      <sensor name="navsat_sensor" type="navsat">
        <gz_frame_id>base_link</gz_frame_id>
        <always_on>1</always_on>
        <update_rate>30</update_rate>
      </sensor>
    </link>

    <!-- ============ Right wing rotor (tilting, above the wing) ============ -->
    <!-- Stack, bottom up: wing upper surface +0.0136, pylon +0.010..+0.070,
         motor body +0.0675..+0.1025 (0.035 long), prop disc at +0.11, i.e. 0.0075
         above the motor, the same clearance the tail rotor uses.
         KEEP IN SYNC: tiltrotor_indi::ROTOR_PZ (TiltrotorIndiParams.hpp) is this
         rotor z in FRD, so SDF +0.11 (FLU) == ROTOR_PZ -0.11. -->
    <link name='motor_0'>
      <pose>0.27 -0.35 0.085 0 0 0</pose>
      <inertial>
        <pose>0 0 0 0 0 0</pose>
        <mass>0.05</mass>
        <inertia>
          <ixx>0.0166704</ixx>
          <ixy>0</ixy>
          <ixz>0</ixz>
          <iyy>0.0166704</iyy>
          <iyz>0</iyz>
          <izz>0.0167604</izz>
        </inertia>
      </inertial>
        <enable_wind>true</enable_wind>
      <collision name='motor_0_collision'>
